 7. 🎃 Candy slump 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Halloween candy sales are off to a slow start this year as U.S. consumers grapple with high living costs and eye-popping chocolate prices.

 Sales fell 6.7% in the month ending Oct. 17 compared with the same period last year, according to NielsenIQ, a market research firm. Sales were down 11.7% in September, erasing preseason gains Halloween candy enjoyed the previous two years, AP reports. Go deeper. 

 
 
